WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
Donald Trump has pushed civil asset forfeiture,

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:04.780
which he supports, back in the news.

00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:06.920
"We've got a state senator in Texas"

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.629
"He was was talking about introducing"

00:00:08.629 --> 00:00:11.180
"legislation to require conviction before"

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.320
"we can receive the forfeiture money."

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.240
"Want to give his name?"

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.580
"I'll destroy his career."

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.540
Here are 3 reasons why civil asset

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.220
forfeiture laws need to be reformed now.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:27.500
Civil asset forfeiture allows cops and

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.419
federal agencies, such as the FBI, to

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:32.500
seize cash and property of suspected criminals.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:33.800
But it doesn't require them to

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:35.910
bring any charges against their targets

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.100
or even show that they were in any way

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:39.780
involved with wrongdoing.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.840
In 2014 for instance

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:42.900
a Philadelphia couple had

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:44.940
their house seized after police arrested

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.280
their son for possessing $40

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.809
of heroin while living there.

00:00:48.809 --> 00:00:50.891
The parents weren't charged with any crime

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.360
but in Pennsylvania and many other states

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.920
owners have seized property must

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.590
prove their innocence to get their stuff back.

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:02.579
In many cases, the agency that seizes

00:01:02.579 --> 00:01:04.350
property and cash gets to keep a big

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.240
chunk of it to fund purchases of

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:08.670
equipment and pay personnel costs.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.000
In Mississippi, in 2015, state narcotics officers

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.160
alone seized 4 million dollars

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.560
in cash, cars, and even couches.

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.960
In the Magnolia state, cops only get to keep

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.800
80 percent of the value of seized assets

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.780
but in 26 States law enforcement

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.240
gets to keep 100 percent of their haul

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.320
giving them an incentive to

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:28.950
grab as much as possible

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.380
especially since it's time-consuming and expensive

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.620
for defendants to go to court.

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:37.799
Although most states do their best to

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:40.079
hide how much civil forfeiture goes on

00:01:40.079 --> 00:01:42.600
it's an increasingly unpopular practice

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.520
because it's so obviously contravenes

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.280
basic notions of justice.

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:49.040
Even in deep-red states, polls routinely show massive

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.760
majorities in favor of reform

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.480
once voters understand just how unfair and

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:55.720
non-transparent the process is.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.680
In fact when President Trump threatened to

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:00.600
destroy the career of a Texas state senator

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.740
he could have been referring to

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:03.680
any of 4 politicians—

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:05.920
3 Republicans and a Democrat

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:06.960
who were deeply involved

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.360
in reform efforts.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:10.960
Civil asset forfeiture reform is an idea

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:12.620
whose time has come

00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:13.960
in Texas and elsewhere

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.560
whether Donald Trump is ready

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.720
or not.

